# Git normalises line endings on commit; the working copy follows the platform.
# Without this, core.autocrlf on Windows checks files out as CRLF while Prettier
# (endOfLine: "lf" by default) checks for LF — so `format:check` fails locally on
# files it passes on in CI. Pinning text files to LF makes the two agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
